#
# One-shot IMEI provisioning. Reads the read-only traceability
# partition, validates both IMEIs and compares them with the modem's current
# NV 550 value. With --write it then writes NV 550 for both subscriptions and
# reads it back. It never touches the partition.
# It runs at every boot, as stock tctd does: activating a slot (fastboot
# --set-active, every OTA) makes the bootloader restore the modem's file system
# from its golden copy, which has no IMEI, so NV 550 must be written again.
# It logs booleans to logcat (tag imeiprovd), never an identifier, sets only
# vendor.diamaneos.imei.status and opens no non-QRTR socket besides the log and
# property sockets (see docs/imei-provisioning.md).
#
# - Own vendor user/group (config.fs), no supplementary groups, no capabilities
#   (an empty capabilities list drops them all for a non-root user).
# - oneshot: runs once per boot and exits. init does not restart it.
# - disabled, started only by the system_ext trigger in imeiprovd-control.rc,
#   because a vendor init trigger cannot gate on persistent-properties readiness.
# The modem's QRTR node is the one the IMS product pins (ims-product.mk). Only
# a TCL QMI service on that node is used.
service vendor.imeiprovd /vendor/bin/imeiprovd --write ${ro.vendor.diamaneos.ims.modem_node}
    class main
    user vendor_imeiprov
    group vendor_imeiprov
    capabilities
    oneshot
    disabled
